{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For as a man disciplines his son</b> — that he places upon him, for his own good, the yoke of discipline, as it is said (Proverbs 19:18), \"Discipline your son, for there is hope, and do not set your soul on putting him to death\" — so HaShem your Elohim disciplines you first through the affliction of the wilderness and the trial of the manna, so that the goodness of the land and its fruits may be sweet to your soul. Therefore it says afterward (Deuteronomy 8:7), \"For HaShem your Elohim is bringing you to a good land.\""], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:45.289743267Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}